  i Negating the whole call hides the condition that is actually checked. Calling every() with a negated callback function gives the same result and is easier to read.
  
  i Remove the ! before the call, use every() instead, and negate the value that the callback function returns.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

